{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01082",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.88,
      "end_seconds": 3.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "Okay, morning, come on through."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 4.39,
      "end_seconds": 5.38,
      "duration_seconds": 0.99,
      "text": "Hi there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.77,
      "end_seconds": 10.74,
      "duration_seconds": 3.97,
      "text": "Sorry about the wait, we're running a bit behind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 11.59,
      "end_seconds": 19.29,
      "duration_seconds": 7.7,
      "text": "Oh, um, that's fine. I was just reading something on my phone."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.38,
      "end_seconds": 23.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "What would you like to start with today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 25.37,
      "end_seconds": 34.73,
      "duration_seconds": 9.36,
      "text": "Um, uh, mainly a blocked ear. There's a couple of other things, but that's the main one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 35.47,
      "end_seconds": 38.67,
      "duration_seconds": 3.2,
      "text": "What's the timeline, when did it begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 40.49,
      "end_seconds": 43.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.41,
      "text": "I've had it since last Tuesday."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 44.23,
      "end_seconds": 46.95,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "Ah. Is there anything else with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 48.33,
      "end_seconds": 73.73,
      "duration_seconds": 25.4,
      "text": "When it starts I tend to get muffled hearing on one side as well. I mean, and there's a feeling of fullness as well, about a week now. Sorry, what was I saying, about muffled hearing on one side, about a six out of ten."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 74.4,
      "end_seconds": 76.77,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "Has there been any ear pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 77.87,
      "end_seconds": 80.16,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "No, no ear pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 81.63,
      "end_seconds": 85.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.43,
      "text": "Have you had any dizziness, discharge or ringing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 91.45,
      "end_seconds": 94.68,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "Hmm, nope, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 95.51,
      "end_seconds": 98.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "Right, any rashes or skin problems otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 99.74,
      "end_seconds": 103.31,
      "duration_seconds": 3.57,
      "text": "Hmm, nothing on the skin, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 105.13,
      "end_seconds": 108.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "So, now some background about your lifestyle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 109.76,
      "end_seconds": 122.33,
      "duration_seconds": 12.57,
      "text": "My partner and our baby. Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit. I'm a hairdresser, on my feet all day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.59,
      "end_seconds": 126.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "Any past operations I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 127.72,
      "end_seconds": 138.87,
      "duration_seconds": 11.15,
      "text": "Yeah, um, just a triple bypass, eight years ago. A neighbour of mine said I should see someone about it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 146.24,
      "end_seconds": 151.1,
      "duration_seconds": 4.86,
      "text": "What conditions have you been treated for in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 152.14,
      "end_seconds": 162.76,
      "duration_seconds": 10.62,
      "text": "So, I've had heart failure for two years now. I told myself I'd wait and see, and here I am."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 164.21,
      "end_seconds": 165.76,
      "duration_seconds": 1.55,
      "text": "Okay, what else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 167.27,
      "end_seconds": 178.58,
      "duration_seconds": 11.31,
      "text": "Mm, I've had gout for five years now. I didn't want to make a fuss, you know. I, I have heart disease."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 179.7,
      "end_seconds": 187.41,
      "duration_seconds": 7.71,
      "text": "Right, right. Yes, heart failure and gout are known to us, good to have that clear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 196.4,
      "end_seconds": 200.28,
      "duration_seconds": 3.88,
      "text": "So, are there any illnesses in your family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 201.87,
      "end_seconds": 205.38,
      "duration_seconds": 3.51,
      "text": "Right, um, my grandmother had dementia."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 207.24,
      "end_seconds": 211.04,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "Are you taking anything regularly, including from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 212.31,
      "end_seconds": 225.92,
      "duration_seconds": 13.61,
      "text": "I'm on carvedilol, 6.25 milligrams, twice a day for my heart. Febuxostat. I take it 80 milligrams, once a day for the gout."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 230.23,
      "end_seconds": 231.53,
      "duration_seconds": 1.3,
      "text": "Is that long-standing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 232.13,
      "end_seconds": 234.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.23,
      "text": "For about a month."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 234.62,
      "end_seconds": 235.53,
      "duration_seconds": 0.91,
      "text": "Hm, okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 236.2,
      "end_seconds": 248.07,
      "duration_seconds": 11.87,
      "text": "I'm, I'm on clopidogrel, 75 milligrams, once a day for the stent. Before this I was on metoprolol; that's been stopped."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 253.45,
      "end_seconds": 255.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.53,
      "text": "Have you got any known allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 259.22,
      "end_seconds": 265.08,
      "duration_seconds": 5.86,
      "text": "Amoxicillin. I come out in... well, a rash all over."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.57,
      "end_seconds": 273.25,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "Let me get the readings out of the way."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 286.37,
      "end_seconds": 289.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "That's it, just a little longer..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 304.72,
      "end_seconds": 312.24,
      "duration_seconds": 7.52,
      "text": "Okay: temperature 36.7, SpO2 97 percent on room air, heart rate 85, pressure 122 over 72."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 313.56,
      "end_seconds": 315.32,
      "duration_seconds": 1.76,
      "text": "Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 316.01,
      "end_seconds": 319.57,
      "duration_seconds": 3.56,
      "text": "I'll explain what these mean in a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 320.62,
      "end_seconds": 324.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.87,
      "text": "I'll examine you in a second, make yourself comfortable."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 326.27,
      "end_seconds": 329.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "Alright, tell me if that's sore."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 340.34,
      "end_seconds": 344.32,
      "duration_seconds": 3.98,
      "text": "There's a lot of wax blocking the right ear canal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 344.87,
      "end_seconds": 345.97,
      "duration_seconds": 1.1,
      "text": "Okay, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 349.28,
      "end_seconds": 352.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "Good, you can sit up again."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 361.09,
      "end_seconds": 370.04,
      "duration_seconds": 8.95,
      "text": "Right, here's what I'm thinking. The most likely explanation is earwax blocking the ear. We shouldn't forget a middle ear fluid."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 375.49,
      "end_seconds": 378.93,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "What are the odds it's serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 380.62,
      "end_seconds": 392.59,
      "duration_seconds": 11.97,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with earwax blocking the ear do well once it's treated properly. I think ear irrigation makes sense here, for wax."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 393.36,
      "end_seconds": 395.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.0,
      "text": "Is that done today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 396.36,
      "end_seconds": 407.13,
      "duration_seconds": 10.77,
      "text": "Use the olive oil drops for a week and then we'll syringe the ear. Right, that's the plan. Do you want to ask me anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 408.3,
      "end_seconds": 412.47,
      "duration_seconds": 4.17,
      "text": "Yeah, no, that's all. Thanks a lot."
    }
  ]
}